> We use sectoral damage estimates from the PESETA IV project \citepalias{feyen2020climate}, which are generally reported at the combined ``UK~+~Ireland'' level. For each relevant impact channel (coastal flooding, crop productivity, droughts, electricity production, heat and cold mortality, and river floods), PESETA provides both direct (partial-equilibrium) losses and economy-wide losses from a computable general equilibrium (CGE) model. We adopt the CGE-based estimates, including non-market mortality losses where reported, to ensure consistency with our macroeconomic framing.
